p [todo (seq (mapcat mentions program)) seen #{}]\n                 (if-let [n (first todo)]\n                   (if (contains? seen n)\n                     (recur (next todo) seen)\n                     (recur (concat (next todo) (mentions (get by-name n))) (conj seen n)))\n                   seen))]\n    (filterv #(contains? needed (second %)) context-forms)))\n\n\n(defn- context-host-form\n  \"B is ordinary Clojure over the checked-in adaptation. The sole guest\n   outcome intrinsic becomes the equivalent host catch; data primitives and\n   deterministic gensym retain exactly their portable contracts.\"\n\n\n(def ^:private kernel-entries\n  (mapv (fn [entry]\n          (let [s (kernel-symbol entry)]\n            (upstream-fn s) ; load the real aliases and refers before resolving source\n            (assoc entry :symbol s :arities (kernel-arities (get top-forms [(:ns entry) (:name entry)])))))\n        manifest))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-resolve\n  [ns-sym s]\n  (when (symbol? s)\n    (let [n (the-ns (symbol (str/replace (str ns-sym) \"_\" \"-\")))\n          v (ns-resolve n s)]\n      (when (and (var? v) (str/starts-with? (str (:ns (meta v))) \"latte-kernel.\"))\n        (symbol (str (:ns (meta v))) (str (:name (meta v))))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-rewrite\n  \"Resolve library names against their actual upstream namespace, respecting\n   lexical binders and quote. No blanket alias stripping or data rewriting.\"\n  [ns-sym form]\n  (letfn [(bindings [pattern] (set (filter symbol? (tree-seq coll? seq pattern))))\n          (forms [xs bound] (map #(step % bound) xs))\n          (arity\n            [xs bound]\n            (let [[params & body] xs\n                  body (forms body (into bound (bindings params)))\n                  body (if (and (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.syntax) (= 'free-vars (second form))\n                                (= '[def-env t] params))\n                         [(list* 'let '[def-env (if (map? def-env) (:definitions def-env) def-env)] body)]\n                         body)]\n              (list* params body)))\n          (step\n            [x bound]\n   'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse-term-rec 'unparse-term-rec\n   'latte-kernel.norm/install-unfold-implicit! 'install-unfold-implicit\n   'latte-kernel.unparser/install-fundamental-unparsers! 'install-fundamental-unparsers\n   'latte-kernel.unparser/prod-impl-unparser 'prod-impl-unparser})\n\n\n(def ^:private kernel-context-extra-arguments\n  ;; Immutable-context APIs take one explicit context where upstream reads\n  ;; or writes an ambient binding. Raw guest arities remain in the trace.\n  {'unregister-unparser 1 'unparse 1 'register-unparser 1\n   'install-unfold-implicit 1 'install-fundamental-unparsers 1\n   'gate-proof-install-opacity-function 1})\n\n\n(defn- kernel-trace-form\n  \"Append the selected function/arity at body entry, including indirect calls.\n   Only C is instrumented; A/B still run their original fixture paths.\"\n  [form]\n  (if (#{'defn 'defn-} (first form))\n    (let [[op fname & header] form\n          header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) header)\n          trace-arity (fn [[params & body]]\n                        (let [n (if (some #{'&} params)\n                                  [:variadic (.indexOf params '&)] (count params))]\n                          (list* params\n                                 (list 'stream/put! 'gate-execution-trace (list 'quote [fname n]))\n                                 body)))]\n      (list* op fname (if (vector? (first header))\n                        (trace-arity header) (map trace-arity header))))\n    form))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-executed-arity?\n  [row symbol n]\n  (let [names (remove nil? [(kernel-guest-name symbol)\n                            (get kernel-context-integration-names symbol)])\n        paths (set (for [fname names]\n                     [fname (if (number? n)\n                              (+ n (get kernel-context-extra-arguments fname 0)) n)]))]\n    (every? (fn [lane] (some paths (get-in row [lane :executed-calls])))\n            [:c-walker :c-semantic])))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-compile\n  [fixture]\n  (let [call (kernel-c-program fixture)\n        forms (kernel-closure call)\n        program (into ['(def gate-execution-trace (stream/make 1000000))]\n                      (concat (map kernel-trace-form forms) [call]))\n        program (into (yang/library-for program) program)\n        opts (update arg-vector-opts :native into\n                     (map (fn [[op profile]] [(clojure.core/symbol \"stream\" (name op)) profile])\n                          module/stream-profiles))\n        ast (yang/compile-program program true opts)\n        missing (unbound-ast-symbols ast program)]\n    (if (seq missing)\n      {:status :blocked :phase :admission :blocked-by (vec (sort missing))\n       :owners (into {} (for [s missing]\n                          [s (mapv second (filter #(some #{s} (tree-seq coll? seq %)) program))]))}\n      {:status :compiled :ast ast :forms forms})))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-c\n  [compiled lane]\n  (if (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n    (assoc (kernel-attempt\n             #(let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n                              (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 4000000)\n                    v (vm/value machine)\n                    ref (get-in machine [:store 'gate-execution-trace])\n                    handle (get-in machine [:resources (:id ref)])]\n                (when-not (and (vm/halted? machine) handle)\n                  (throw (ex-info \"Execution trace did not complete\" {:lane lane})))\n                {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))\n                 :executed-calls (tu/drain handle)}))\n           :lane lane)\n    (assoc compiled :lane lane)))\n\n\n(deftest test-kernel-proof-fresh-supply\n  (testing \"explicit have types advance the supply; inferred types and prior contexts are preserved\"\n    (doseq [[name next-name] [['h 'h2] ['_ '_]]\n            [ty allocations] [['A 1] ['_ 0]]]\n      (let [fixture\n            {:call\n             (walk/postwalk-replace\n               {'H name 'H2 next-name 'TY ty}\n               '(let [k0 env\n                      [s1 [k1 ctx1 deps1 uses1]]\n                      (latte-kernel.proof/elab-have k0 '[[A ✳] [x A]] [] {} 'H 'TY 'x {})\n                      [s2 [k2 ctx2 deps2 uses2]]\n                      (latte-kernel.proof/elab-have k1 ctx1 deps1 uses1 'H2 'TY 'x {})\n                      [s3 [k3 ctx3 deps3 uses3]]\n                      (latte-kernel.proof/elab-declare k2 ctx2 deps2 uses2 'z 'A {})\n                      [s4 [k4 ctx4 deps4 uses4]]\n                      (latte-kernel.proof/elab-have k3 ctx3 deps3 uses3 '_ 'A 'z {})]\n                  [[s1 s2 s3 s4]\n                   [(:fresh k0) (:fresh k1) (:fresh k2) (:fresh k3) (:fresh k4)]\n                   (mapv (fn [k] (count (second (:definitions k)))) [k0 k1 k2 k3 k4])\n                   (= ctx1 '[[A ✳] [x A]]) (= ctx1 ctx2)]))}\n            expected [[:ok :ok :ok :ok] [0 allocations (* 2 allocations)\n                                         (inc (* 2 allocations)) (+ 2 (* 2 allocations))]\n                      (if (= name '_) [0 0 0 0 0] [0 1 2 2 2])\n                      true true]\n            compiled (kernel-compile fixture)]\n        (is (= {:value expected} (:outcome (kernel-b fixture))))\n        (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n          (let [c (kernel-c compiled lane)]\n            (is (= [:yin.k/ok expected] (:outcome c)) (str name \" \" lane \" \" c)))))))\n  (testing \"the proof loop carries the returned supply to the next step and qed\"\n    (doseq [[script fresh]\n            [['((:have h A x {}) (:have h2 A x {}) (:qed x {})) 2]\n             ['((:have _ A x {}) (:have _ A x {}) (:qed x {})) 2]\n             ['((:declare z A {}) (:have h A z {}) (:declare w A {}) (:have h2 A w {}) (:qed w {})) 4]]]\n      (let [fixture {:call (list 'let ['r (list 'latte-kernel.proof/elab-proof 'env ''[[A ✳] [x A]]\n                                                (list 'quote script))]\n                                 '[(first r) (:fresh (first (second r))) (:fresh env) (:definitions env)])}\n            expected [:ok fresh 0 [{} {}]]\n            compiled (kernel-compile fixture)]\n        (is (= {:value expected} (:outcome (kernel-b fixture))))\n        (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n          (is (= [:yin.k/ok expected] (:outcome (kernel-c compiled lane))) (str lane))))))\n  (testing \"check-proof keeps the rebuilt context under its own def-env' binding\"\n    ;; Observe the context passed to the final comparison: check-proof's public\n    ;; result contains only the proof term and type, so it cannot expose :fresh.\n    (with-redefs [kernel-sources\n                  (assoc kernel-sources 'gate-norm-beta-eq?\n                         '(defn gate-norm-beta-eq?\n                            [def-env ctx t1 t2]\n                            (= 1 (:fresh def-env))))]\n      (let [fixture {:call '(latte-kernel.proof/check-proof env '[[A ✳] [x A]] 't 'A '[[:qed x {}]])}\n            expected [:ok ['x 'A]]\n            compiled (kernel-compile fixture)]\n        (is (= {:value expected} (:outcome (kernel-b fixture))))\n        (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n          (is (= [:yin.k/ok expected] (:outcome (kernel-c compiled lane))) (str lane)))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private kernel-named-integrations\n  ;; Only these named integrations may contribute observed transitive calls.\n  ;; Static dependencies never establish execution of any arity.\n  #{:unparser-guest-closure :implicit-typed-closure :implicit-throwing-closure\n    :check-assume-have-discharge :parse-to-normalize-to-type\n    :h3-2-elab-inferred-anonymous :h3-2-elab-discharge-states\n    :h3-3-readable-term-2 :h3-3-readable-term-3 :h3-3-unregister-unparser\n    :fundamental-install-use :unfold-install-use :opacity-install-use})\n\n\n(def ^:private kernel-unexercised-reasons\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice9_unexercised.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-exercise-entries\n  [inventory fixtures results]\n  (vec\n    (for [{:keys [symbol arities disposition]} inventory\n          :when (= :admitted disposition)\n          n arities\n          :let [direct (vec (for [[fixture row] (map vector fixtures results)\n                                  :when (and (= :pass (:status row))\n                                             (kernel-executed-arity? row symbol n)\n                                             (= symbol (first (:call fixture)))\n                                             (= n (count (rest (:call fixture)))))]\n                              (:id fixture)))\n                integration (vec (for [row results\n                                       :when (and (= :pass (:status row))\n# Slice 9 kernel differential gate: execution evidence correction\n\nThe gate on the hardening line is **blocked**. The architect denied the prior\n165/165 closure claim because membership in a static dependency closure did\nnot prove execution of every arity. That claim is withdrawn. The gate retains\nits final assertion `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))`; missing execution\nevidence must fail that assertion.\n\nThe 106-fixture corpus has **100 passing agreements, two recorded deviations\n(`elab-after-qed`, `check-after-qed`), two blocked fixtures, and two recorded\nupstream failures.** The four narrowly recorded exception dispositions remain\ndeclared departures, not agreements. No upstream or `src/cljc/` source changes\nare made by H3-0. Admission is unchanged: 155 bindings (146 admitted, 9\nexcluded) and 175 candidate function/arities (165 admitted, 10 excluded).\n\nRecorded executions establish **107/165** admitted arities: 39 directly\nand 68 through named integrations. The other **58**, including `parse/1`,\nremain uncredited. The declared departures are carried by the versioned\n[`slice9_declarations.edn`](slice9_declarations.edn) (provenance `ea18c8e4^`),\nrevalidated on every refresh by the representation-aware classifier: the\nguest `:meta` value may be a pre-adoption raw closure or the admitted §8.10\ndescriptor; structurally invalid descriptors and any payload, message, script\nor call mismatch refuse (descriptor authenticity itself is the compiler's\nadmission witness upstream of the outcome). The corrected counts and remaining arities\nare recorded in [`slice9_evidence.edn`](slice9_evidence.edn) and\n[`slice9_unexercised.edn`](slice9_unexercised.edn). The residual consumers in\n[`fixture_closure.edn`](fixture_closure.edn) retain their concrete expected\noutcomes; they do not establish closure of the full inventory, and their\ncount (20) predates the re-derivation — the live unexercised set is the\n58-name list.\n\n## Consumer evidence\n\n- `mkenv` preserves a nonempty global environment and creates empty locals.\n- `beta-red`, `delta-normalize`, and `delta-normalize-local` have explicit\n  entry fixtures and missing-reference rejections. The local wrapper also\n  exercises explicit local definitions and their precedence over an ambient\n  namespace definition.\n- `install-unfold-implicit!` installs into both isolated upstream atoms on A.\n  B/C return an updated immutable context, used by both the delta wrapper and\n  NBE. Both normalizers read the same installed extension. An installed\n  refusing extension propagates its original error data.\n- `install-opacity-function` starts from a refusing policy, explicitly installs\n  the working policy, then enters the original proof dispatcher through\n  opaque/transparent steps and qed. A duplicate opaque step rejects. A uses\n  an isolated namespace and host-local Var policy; B/C thread immutable\n  definition updates through the explicit context.\n- `install-fundamental-unparsers!` starts from an empty registry, installs the\n  fundamental product unparser, then unparses nested implications. Dependent\n  products and atoms remain unchanged. Direct `prod-impl-unparser` fixtures\n  also verify its `[term false]` refusal result.\n- `exists-kw?`, `term?`, `pair?`, and `vectorn?` include false results.\n  `bound-vars` distinguishes a bound occurrence from entirely free variables.\n  These fixtures preserve upstream behavior, including its shallow term\n  validator and the use of `vector` rather than `vector?` in utility predicates.\n- `proper-type?` enters each arity separately. Unknown variables throw;\n  a well-typed term whose inferred type is not a sort returns false.\n- `show-deftype` checks definition, axiom, theorem, implicit, and unknown\n  labels. It depends only on portable record-kind predicates and returns a\n  string. Host pprint and stdout functions remain excluded.\n- `safe-get` covers successful lookup, missing keys, stored false, and stored\n  nil. The latter three all reject upstream. `vremove` removes every match,\n  preserves a no-match vector, and propagates a predicate's domain exception.\n\n`mkenv`, `appify`, and `bound-vars` have no domain rejection in the pinned\nsource; the fixtures preserve their constructor, empty-input, and empty-set\nresults instead of manufacturing refusals. A refused product rewrite is\nidentified by its explicit modification flag, not mistaken for an exception.\n\nThe pinned local delta wrapper has a narrower portability scope than its\ndocstring suggests: `delta-step` drops `local?` when calling `delta-reduction`\non a reference. Consequently upstream can resolve a global or host namespace\ndefinition on that path. The global-result fixture preserves this behavior;\nthe namespace fixture supplies a local definition that shadows the ambient\none. The guest boundary still requires explicit definitions and has no host\nnamespace lookup capability. This round does not repair upstream or claim\nagreement for ambient-only resolution.\n\n## Acceptance counting\n\nEvery selected guest function body appends `[guest-function arity]` to an\nexplicit diagnostic stream at entry. Instrumentation covers all arities of\nthe functions supplied to each fixture, including higher-order calls through\nregistries and extension closures. Each C lane creates its own stream.\nAfter the VM halts, the harness reads that stream through its own\ncursor, preserving the fixture's original outcome and exception payload.\nA/B remain uninstrumented. Raw ordered call records are retained under\n`:c-walker :executed-calls` and `:c-semantic :executed-calls` for every completed\nfixture. The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions per\nlane. The instrumented fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound because\nbody-entry stream writes add guest instructions. Reading the completed\ndiagnostic stream is harness work after halt. This is an instrumentation\nbudget change, not a new performance acceptance claim.\n\nPassing direct fixtures contribute only their original function/argument\ncount, and only with matching body-entry records in both C lanes. Passing\nnamed integrations contribute only exact arities recorded in both C lanes.\nStatic dependency membership contributes no credit. Full branch coverage is\nnot required. Context adapter identities and explicit extra context arguments\nare recorded in the evidence; each observed guest arity is checked against\nthat mapping individually, never against all arities of its function.\n\nOnly `:pass` fixture rows contribute exercise evidence. Recorded upstream\nfailures and deviations do not contribute. Any admitted arity without a\npassing direct or named integration execution path blocks the gate.\n\nThe accounting regression first failed against the old implementation: it\ncredited the deliberately uncalled arity and accepted missing C-lane traces.\nIt now requires both traces and leaves unused arities uncredited. A second\nregression replaces the adapted `parse/1` body in memory with an unconditional\nerror, then runs `:parse-to-normalize-to-type`. A/B and both C lanes still\npass; both C traces record `parse/2` and no `parse/1`, and the counter leaves\n`parse/1` uncredited. Every credited path is also checked against the recorded\nexecutions of its named fixture. See\n[`slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt`](slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt).\n\n## Recorded portability boundaries\n\nThe two `:recorded-deviation` rows remain `:elab-after-qed` and\n`:check-after-qed`. Upstream embeds `clojure.core/meta`, a host function, in\nexception data; C carries a guest closure. The original outcomes, comparison\nflags, exact payload guards, and evidence pointers remain intact. Both rows\nare listed in `:recorded-portability-boundaries` in the summary. Neither is\nreported as agreement.\n\n## Recorded upstream failures\n\n`:typing-ascription` still reaches the upstream declaration\n`type-of-ascribe`, which has no definition. A raises its original unbound-fn\nexception; B/C retain the explicit branch-local refusal.\n\n`:compile-malformed` still passes scalar proof input `[42]`. A/B raise the\noriginal native sequence exception; C retains its portable sequence refusal.\n\nThese two rows have the distinct disposition `:recorded-upstream-failure` and\nare listed in `:recorded-upstream-failures`. Their original A/B/C records and\nfalse agreement flags remain available. The disposition checks the exact\nfixture ID, input call, exception class/message, B outcome, and both completed\nC outcomes. Changed calls, IDs, or C payloads are tested to refuse the\ndisposition. Any other execution failure remains a blocker. No upstream fix,\naccepted-negative claim, or equality projection is introduced for these rows.\n\n## Verification\n\nAn independent audit re-derives the credited arities and fixture paths from\nthe two raw C traces. Kondo reports zero errors and warnings. The full oracle\nruns 26 tests and 1,697 assertions with exactly one failure and no errors:\nits retained `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))` closure assertion. The\nunexercised arities — **58** under the current accounting, including\n`parse/1` — therefore continue to block acceptance. Verification results are\nrecorded in [`slice9_verification.edn`](slice9_verification.edn), with command\noutputs beside it.\n`yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!` explicitly regenerates\nboth execution evidence and the remaining-arity inventory; normal tests do\nnot write them. Evidence retains the pinned upstream revision, compiler\ndigest, runtime, instruction budget, per-fixture outcomes, diagnostic traces,\ndependency graph, admission inventory, credited paths, and all four recorded\nexception dispositions.\n\nThe append-only correction in [`known-gaps.md`](../../../docs/agents/known-gaps.md)\nrecords that host Clojure turns a thrown string into `ClassCastException`,\ncaught by `catch Exception` but not `catch ExceptionInfo`. Portable `try` binds\nthe error payload without equivalent runtime class handling; this guest/host\ngap remains declared.\n\nExecution scope is both C evaluators on the JVM. This correction does not\nclaim renewed architect sign-off or Node/Dart verification, and the blocked\ngate does not authorize program closure or merge.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'Gate S|exact mapped arity|H3-6|164/165' docs/plan* docs/spec* 2>/dev/null | head -100; rg -n 'registered-definition' vendor -g '*.clj' 2>/dev/null | head -20; sed -n '280,345p' test/yang/latte_oracle/h3_3_fixture_family.md; sed -n '1,115p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'Gate S|exact mapped arity|H3-6|164/165' docs/plan* docs/spec* 2>/dev/null | head -100; rg -n 'registered-definition' vendor -g '*.clj' 2>/dev/null | head -20; sed -n '280,345p' test/yang/latte_oracle/h3_3_fixture_family.md; sed -n '1,115p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md\"","aggregated_output":"zsh:1: no matches found: docs/plan*\n## 4. The family\n\nProposed corpus rows are shown in the corpus's EDN shape (A form; the\nharness derives B/C, using `:guest-call` where present). New IDs are\nmarked †. Every predicted A outcome below is A-verified (§0); predicted\nB/C outcomes are the same value unless stated, derived per §3.\n\n### 4.1 defenv predicates\n\nF1† `:h3-3-axiom-true` — primary witness for `axiom?/1` (direct):\n\n```clojure\n{:id :h3-3-axiom-true,\n :call (latte-kernel.defenv/axiom? (latte-kernel.defenv/->Axiom (quote a) [] 0 (quote T)))}\n```\n\nExpected A/B/C: `true`. Required trace: `[gate-defenv-axiom? 1]` in both\nC lanes. The two false companions are refusal rows in §5 (R1); they trace\nthe same record and, negativity notwithstanding, would also credit\n`axiom?/1` under the harness as it stands if they pass (§5.1). F1\nremains the designated primary witness in this design's accounting.\n\nF2† `:h3-3-registered-definition-ambient` — designed witness for\n`registered-definition?/1`, **non-crediting** (§7):\n\n```clojure\n{:id :h3-3-registered-definition-ambient,\n :call (latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? (quote gate-no-such-definition)),\n :guest-call (registered-definition? env (quote gate-no-such-definition))}\n```\n\nExpected A: `false` — the name is in neither the ambient `empty-env`\nnor any namespace the A leg can resolve (the name is chosen to resolve\nnowhere; if a future namespace interns it, this prediction breaks and\nthe fixture must be renamed, never re-expected). Expected B/C: `false`\n(context fetch on the initial context misses both maps). There is no\nrequired trace for credit, because this row credits nothing: its guest\ncall is predicted to trace `[registered-definition? 2]` and\n`[registered-definition? 3]` in both C lanes (§3), but\n`kernel-executed-arity?` for upstream `/1` seeks\n`[gate-defenv-registered-definition? 1]`, no bare-name mapping exists,\nand §7 withdraws the +1 trace-table mapping an earlier draft proposed\n(it is not arity-safe). The gate-wrapper `/1` the direct route would\notherwise use is arity-broken against the context signature (§3), so\nno ordinary fixture credits this arity; the gate stays honestly\n`:blocked` on it. The non-symbol refusal companion is R2 in §5. A `true` case for `/1` is deliberately **not**\ndesigned: on A it could only be produced by namespace resolution (the\nambient env is empty by definition), which B/C expressly do not have —\nsuch a row would be a manufactured mismatch, not a fixture.\n\n### 4.2 nbe\n\nF3† `:h3-3-nbe-evaluation-one` — primary witness for `evaluation/1`\n(direct):\n\n```clojure\n{:id :h3-3-nbe-evaluation-one,\n :call (latte-kernel.nbe/evaluation (quote [(λ [a ✳] a) b]))}\n```\n\nExpected A/B/C: `b`. The term fully applies, so the host function the\nbinder branch builds is consumed internally and never appears in the\nresult (§3); a binder-returning term would embed a host `fn` and is\nexcluded by design. Required trace: `[gate-nbe-evaluation 1]`, plus\nredundant `[gate-nbe-evaluation 4]`. Companion `:h3-3-nbe-evaluation-var`\n(`(quote a)` → `a`, same traces) is a redundant second direct row; the\n(ns yang.latte-oracle-test\n  \"Pinned upstream LaTTe differential harness, slices 1-9 of the Yang gap\n   program. A executes the original library on Clojure. B executes explicit\n   portability source on Clojure; C compiles it through Yang for the walker\n   and semantic VMs. Slice 9 fails closed on the full kernel corpus. The\n   legacy classifier records historical blockers;\n   the context module additionally checks free-symbol admission before C.\n   Adaptations, operation sequences and scope departures live beside the\n   manifest in yang/latte_oracle/.\"\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [clojure.tools.reader :as r]\n            [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as rows-support]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n\n\n(def ^:private manifest\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn- ns-declaration-aliases\n  \"Alias -> full ns symbol, taken from the file's own (ns ...) declaration —\n   never invented: ::alias/kw must read as :that.real.ns/kw.\"\n  [ns-form]\n  (let [alias-map (atom {})\n        consume-spec (fn [spec]\n                       (when (sequential? spec)\n                         (let [lib (first spec)]\n                           (loop [xs (rest spec)]\n                             (when (seq xs)\n                               (if (= :as (first xs))\n                                 (do (swap! alias-map assoc (second xs) lib)\n                                     (recur (drop 2 xs)))\n                                 (recur (next xs))))))))]\n    (loop [clauses (rest (rest ns-form))]\n      (when (seq clauses)\n        (let [clause (first clauses)]\n          (if (and (seq? clause) (= :require (first clause)))\n            (do (loop [reqs (next clause)]\n                  (let [spec (first reqs)]\n                    (when (and (not (nil? spec)) (not (keyword? spec)))\n                      (consume-spec spec)\n                      (recur (next reqs)))))\n                (recur (next clauses)))\n            (recur (next clauses))))))\n    @alias-map))\n\n\n(defn- read-forms\n  \"Read one latte-kernel source file with reader conditionals resolved for\n   :clj, ::alias/kw keywords resolved against the file's own ns declaration,\n   and ::kw resolved against the file's own namespace — so the C leg compiles\n   the same keyword identities the upstream A leg runs.\"\n  [ns-sym]\n  (let [f (io/resource (str (str/replace (name ns-sym) \".\" \"/\") \".cljc\"))\n        pr (rt/source-logging-push-back-reader (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader f)) 1 (str f))\n        ns-form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)\n        declared-name (second ns-form)\n        aliases (ns-declaration-aliases ns-form)]\n    (binding [r/*alias-map* aliases\n              *ns* (the-ns (create-ns declared-name))]\n      (loop [acc []]\n        (let [form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)]\n          (if (= form ::eof) acc (recur (conj acc form))))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private all-forms\n  (into {} (map (fn [ns-sym] [ns-sym (read-forms ns-sym)])\n                (distinct (map :ns manifest)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private top-forms\n  (into {} (map (fn [{:keys [ns kind name]}]\n                  [[ns name] (first (filter #(and (seq? %)\n                                                  (= kind (first %))\n                                                  (= name (second %)))\n                                            (get all-forms ns)))]))\n        manifest))\n\n\n(def ^:private scanned-symbols\n  #{'loop 'recur 'case 'throw 'ex-info 'atom 'swap! 'reset! 'lazy-seq 'gensym\n    'apply 'comp 'partial 'reduced 'reduce 'map 'mapv 'filter 'remove 'into\n    'concat 'merge 'str 'symbol 'keyword 'vector 'seq 'nth 'nthnext 'assoc-in\n    'count 'name 'when-let 'if-let 'when-some 'if-some 'cond})\n\n\n(defn- walk-symbols\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (seq? form) (if (and (= 'quote (first form)) (= 2 (count form)))\n                  #{}\n                  (mapcat walk-symbols form))\n    (vector? form) (mapcat walk-symbols form)\n    (map? form) (mapcat walk-symbols (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\n    (set? form) (mapcat walk-symbols form)\n    (symbol? form) (if (namespace form) #{} #{form})\n    :else #{}))\n---\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\n---\n\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\n\n## Domain Scope\n\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\n\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\n\n## Core Responsibilities\n\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\n\n## Delegation Prompt Template\n\n```text\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\n# Task: <Task Name>\n\nRole: Lead System Architect\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\n\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\n\nRead first:\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\n- <target-design-file>\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\n\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
